    base = "parametric-math-kernel-v0";
    rev_note = "v0.12-VV..AAB (div-math): integrating capstone of the div-math kernel. Imports all forty-three div-math owners (numeric-evaluator, number-theory, rational, linear-equation, combinatorics, modular-arithmetic, polynomial, quadratic-equation, statistics, matrix, sequence-series, set-theory, boolean-logic, base-conversion, geometry, complex-number, bitwise, continued-fraction, graph-theory, interval-arithmetic, probability, calculus, chinese-remainder, vector, prime-sieve, roman-numerals, digit-operations, gray-code, collatz, decimal-expansion, logarithm, partition, figurate-numbers, pascal-triangle, factoradic, euler-totient, josephus, perfect-power, stern-brocot, lucas-sequence, ackermann, bell-numbers, pythagorean-triples, tetrahedral-numbers, triangle-classify, harmonic-numbers, kaprekar, egyptian-fraction, happy-numbers, narcissistic-numbers, amicable-numbers) and exposes a self-describing mathKernelInventory, a single applyMathKernel dispatcher routing on `kernel_domain`, and a mathKernelSelfAudit. Adds no new math -- only the unifying inventory and dispatcher. Every new owner is folded in as it lands (XX: boolean-logic, YY: base-conversion, AAA: geometry, AAB: complex-number, AAC: bitwise, AAD: continued-fraction, AAE: graph-theory, AAF: interval-arithmetic, AAG: probability, AAH: calculus, AAI: chinese-remainder, AAJ: vector, AAK: prime-sieve, AAL: roman-numerals, AAM: digit-operations, AAN: gray-code, AAO: collatz, AAP: decimal-expansion, AAQ: logarithm, AAR: partition, AAS: figurate-numbers, AAT: pascal-triangle, AAU: factoradic, AAX: euler-totient, AAY: josephus, AAZ: perfect-power, ABA: stern-brocot, ABB: lucas-sequence, ABC: ackermann, ABD: bell-numbers, ABE: pythagorean-triples, ABF: tetrahedral-numbers, ABG: triangle-classify, ABH: harmonic-numbers, ABI: kaprekar, ABJ: egyptian-fraction, ABK: happy-numbers, ABL: narcissistic-numbers, ABM: amicable-numbers). NOT a natural-language front end, NOT yet a registered lens.";
